    "Algorithm2_2": "Output x_t, then use g_t and eta_t to project x_t-eta_t*g_t into V.",
    "Algorithm12_3": "Direction learner receives the original gradient linear loss; magnitude learner receives scalar s_t=<g_t,direction_t>.",
    "Theorem12_16": "For nonzero comparator, total linear regret decomposes exactly into magnitude regret at ||u|| plus ||u|| times direction regret at u/||u||.",
    "Section13_4_Eq13_2": "PDF228/printed216 specifies unit Euclidean ball, x1=0 and eta_t=sqrt2/(2Lsqrt(t)), followed by combined KT/direction guarantee."
