  "hypotheses_checked": [
    "[-1,1] is a nonempty closed convex scalar Euclidean unit ball; x1=0 and u=1 are feasible.",
    "All stepsizes are positive and use the actual round t, including zero-gradient rounds.",
    "Each linear loss is convex, finite, subdifferentiable globally and at most1-Lipschitz; its unique subgradient is g_t with |g_t|<=1.",
    "Gradients are predetermined and valid at any combined learner output, so the direction input sequence is admissible under Algorithm12.3.",
    "Comparator direction1 has norm1 and comes from any positive scalar combined comparator; no infeasible direction is used."
